D1  claim S-6: Game-perp makes (iv') trivial at a challenge-refused rho,
    Game-prefix does not.  Built explicitly.
    masked prefix     per-rho view TV: prefix=0 perp=0 | adaptive TV: prefix=0 perp=0
    leaky prefix      per-rho view TV: prefix=1 perp=0 | adaptive TV: prefix=1 perp=0
  VERDICT: claim S-6 CONFIRMED and made exact -- for the SAME protocol,
           hypothesis (iv') holds at every rho under Game perp and FAILS at the
           challenge-refused rho under Game prefix, and the adaptive
           conclusion follows the hypothesis.  Game perp is load-bearing,
           so GAP S-3 (M-9 has no production code) is a real obligation.

    Does the ABORT PROBABILITY itself leak under Game-perp?  A protocol whose
    prefix is perfectly masked but whose refusal probability is
    witness-dependent:
      prefix perfectly masked, refusal rate w/4.  Game-perp adaptive TV = 1/2
      = exactly the gap in refusal rate.  The abort INDICATOR is inside the
      Game-perp view; nothing in the lemma hides it.  So the memo's 'liveness,
      not distance' line for the challenge-driven class is valid ONLY because
      that class is a function of rho ALONE -- if any of the four
      challenge-driven refusals also reads omega or w, it becomes a DISTANCE
      and must join B.  The memo asserts 'functions of rho alone' without a
      line-by-line code check.

